VellumPdf
Copyright © Timothy van der Ham (@Tim81)

This product is an original, independent, clean-room implementation of the
Portable Document Format (PDF). It is implemented from published open
specifications, principally the ISO 32000 family of standards, together with
other open specifications it interoperates with (for example the OpenType and
TrueType font specifications). For barcode symbologies whose governing
standard is patented, it is also implemented from the original patent (for
example US 5,591,956 for Aztec Code). A reference decoder, zxing-cpp, is used
only as an interoperability cross-check in the test suite, never as a source
of implementation; this includes verifying the exact Aztec module-placement
coordinates, since the relevant ISO/IEC 24778 figures are not freely
available. No source code is copied from, and this product is not derived
from, any third-party PDF or barcode library.

